              rdfs:comment "Further clarifies the classification of high-risk AI systems, particularly those listed in Annex III, based on their intended purpose and context of use. Notes: Art. 6(2) is a governance classification rule: it determines whether Annex III systems fall under the high-risk regime. Fairness notions/metrics are used as evidence instruments to support non-discrimination assessment, acceptance testing, and monitoring once the presumption applies (or to substantiate the non-high-risk derogation when claimed)." .


###  https://purl.org/fairops/indiv#Art.71
indiv:Art.71 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                      core:LegalRequirement ,
                      core:ManagementLegalRequirement ;
             ns1:SIO_000068 core:EU_AI_Act ;
             core:isOperationalizedBy indiv:Calibration ,
                                      indiv:CounterfactualFairness ,
                                      indiv:DemographicParity ,
                                      indiv:DiscriminationScore ,
                                      indiv:EqualOpportunity ,
                                      indiv:EqualizedOdds ,
                                      indiv:MatchingConditionalFrequencies ,
                                      indiv:StatisticalParity ,
                                      indiv:TestFairness ;
             core:itsComplianceIsSupportedWith indiv:AugmentedAntidoteData ,
                                               indiv:CalibratedReRanking ,
                                               indiv:ListReAdjustment ,
                                               indiv:ReSamplingProtectedGroup ,
                                               indiv:RegularizationOnANOVA ,
                                               indiv:RegularizationOnValueFairness ,
                                               indiv:UserItemReRanking ;
             rdfs:comment "Establishes an EU database for high-risk AI systems, containing information on systems placed on the market or put into service, including their purpose and key characteristics. Notes: The database can be used to track and analyse fairness-relevant properties across systems." .


###  https://purl.org/fairops/indiv#Art.72.1
indiv:Art.72.1 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                        core:LegalRequirement ,
                        core:ManagementLegalRequirement ;
               ns1:SIO_000068 core:EU_AI_Act ;
               core:isOperationalizedBy indiv:Calibration ,
                                        indiv:CounterfactualFairness ,
                                        indiv:DemographicParity ,
                                        indiv:DiscriminationScore ,
                                        indiv:EqualOpportunity ,
                                        indiv:EqualizedOdds ,
                                        indiv:FairnessThroughAwareness ,
                                        indiv:IndividualFairness ,
                                        indiv:MatchingConditionalFrequencies ,
                                        indiv:StatisticalParity ,
                                        indiv:TestFairness ;
               core:isTriggeredBy core:DerogatoryLanguage ,
                                  core:DisparateSystemPerformance ,
                                  core:ExclusionaryNorms ,
                                  core:FeedbackLoopOverfitting ,
                                  core:Misrepresentation ,
                                  core:Stereotyping ,
                                  core:Toxicity ;
               rdfs:comment "Specifies that providers must systematically collect, document and analyse data relevant to the functioning of high-risk AI systems, including possible risks to fundamental rights, as part of post-market monitoring. Notes: Art. 72(1) is the KPI layer: fairness notions/metrics are used as post-deployment risk indicators and drift signals; techniques are handled under 72(2)." .


###  https://purl.org/fairops/indiv#Art.72.2
indiv:Art.72.2 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                        core:LegalRequirement ,
                        core:ManagementLegalRequirement ;
               ns1:SIO_000068 core:EU_AI_Act ;
               core:isOperationalizedBy indiv:Calibration ,
                                        indiv:CounterfactualFairness ,
                                        indiv:DemographicParity ,
                                        indiv:DiscriminationScore ,
                                        indiv:EqualOpportunity ,
                                        indiv:EqualizedOdds ,
                                        indiv:MatchingConditionalFrequencies ,
                                        indiv:StatisticalParity ,
                                        indiv:TestFairness ;
               core:isTriggeredBy core:DerogatoryLanguage ,
                                  core:DisparateSystemPerformance ,
                                  core:ExclusionaryNorms ,
                                  core:FeedbackLoopOverfitting ,
                                  core:Misrepresentation ,
                                  core:Stereotyping ,
                                  core:Toxicity ;
               core:itsComplianceIsSupportedWith indiv:AugmentedAntidoteData ,
                                                 indiv:CDA ,
                                                 indiv:CalibratedReRanking ,
                                                 indiv:ListReAdjustment ,
                                                 indiv:ReSamplingProtectedGroup ,
                                                 indiv:RegularizationOnANOVA ,
                                                 indiv:RegularizationOnValueFairness ,
                                                 indiv:UserItemReRanking ;
               rdfs:comment "Requires providers to take corrective actions, including necessary updates or withdrawal, when they identify non-compliance or new risks to health, safety or fundamental rights. Notes: Art. 72(2) is the remediation layer: apply updates/rollback/withdrawal; demonstrate risk reduction using the same KPIs defined under 72(1) with versioned evidence." .


###  https://purl.org/fairops/indiv#Art.73
indiv:Art.73 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                      core:LegalRequirement ,
                      core:ManagementLegalRequirement ;
             ns1:SIO_000068 core:EU_AI_Act ;
             core:isOperationalizedBy indiv:Calibration ,
                                      indiv:CounterfactualFairness ,
                                      indiv:DemographicParity ,
                                      indiv:DiscriminationScore ,
                                      indiv:EqualOpportunity ,
                                      indiv:EqualizedOdds ,
                                      indiv:MatchingConditionalFrequencies ,
                                      indiv:StatisticalParity ,
                                      indiv:TestFairness ;
             rdfs:comment "Requires providers to report serious incidents and malfunctioning that constitute a breach of obligations or pose serious risks to health, safety or fundamental rights to competent authorities. Notes: Art. 72(3) is the escalation layer: report serious incidents; triggers can be defined as material KPI breaches or abrupt drift that invalidates prior compliance evidence." .


###  https://purl.org/fairops/indiv#Art.77
indiv:Art.77 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                      core:LegalRequirement ,
                      core:ManagementLegalRequirement ;
             ns1:SIO_000068 core:EU_AI_Act ;
             core:isOperationalizedBy indiv:Calibration ,
                                      indiv:CounterfactualFairness ,
                                      indiv:DemographicParity ,
                                      indiv:DiscriminationScore ,
                                      indiv:EqualOpportunity ,
                                      indiv:EqualizedOdds ,
                                      indiv:FairnessThroughAwareness ,
                                      indiv:IndividualFairness ,
                                      indiv:MatchingConditionalFrequencies ,
                                      indiv:StatisticalParity ,
                                      indiv:TestFairness ;
             core:itsComplianceIsSupportedWith indiv:AddNonToxicExamples ,
                                               indiv:AdversarialFDP ,
                                               indiv:AugmentedAntidoteData ,
                                               indiv:BlocklistDocumentRemoval ,
                                               indiv:CDA ,
                                               indiv:CalibratedReRanking ,
                                               indiv:ControlOffensiveTokens ,
                                               indiv:ListReAdjustment ,
                                               indiv:LogLikeDocumentRemoval ,
                                               indiv:PerceptronForUnawareness ,
                                               indiv:REALTOXICITYPROMPTS ,
                                               indiv:ReSamplingProtectedGroup ,
                                               indiv:RegularizationOnANOVA ,
                                               indiv:RegularizationOnValueFairness ,
                                               indiv:UserItemReRanking ;
             rdfs:comment "Establishes the role and powers of authorities protecting fundamental rights (incl. non-discrimination): they may request necessary documentation/information and, if insufficient to assess risk, ask market surveillance authorities to organise testing. Notes: Enforcement hook: authorities can request documentation and trigger testing; notions/metrics are mapped as reviewable evidence, techniques as corrective options that can be required/verified after findings." .


###  https://purl.org/fairops/indiv#Art.9
indiv:Art.9 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                     core:LegalRequirement ,
                     core:ManagementLegalRequirement ;
            ns1:SIO_000068 core:EU_AI_Act ;
            core:isOperationalizedBy indiv:Calibration ,
                                     indiv:ConditionalStatisticalParity ,
                                     indiv:CounterfactualFairness ,
                                     indiv:DemographicParity ,
                                     indiv:DiscriminationScore ,
                                     indiv:EqualOpportunity ,
                                     indiv:EqualizedOdds ,
                                     indiv:ErrorRateBalance ,
                                     indiv:FairnessThroughAwareness ,
                                     indiv:FalseNegativeErrorRateBalance ,
                                     indiv:FalsePositiveErrorRateBalance ,
                                     indiv:IndividualFairness ,
                                     indiv:MatchingConditionalFrequencies ,
                                     indiv:PredictiveEquality ,
                                     indiv:StatisticalParity ,
                                     indiv:TestFairness ;
            core:isTriggeredBy core:BiasPerpetuation ,
                               core:DerogatoryLanguage ,
                               core:DisparateSystemPerformance ,
                               core:Erasure ,
                               core:ExclusionaryNorms ,
                               core:FeedbackLoopOverfitting ,
                               core:IncompleteHistoricalExamples ,
                               core:Misrepresentation ,
                               core:MisrepresentationsInProductMarketing ,
                               core:PopularItemsOverrecommended ,
                               core:Stereotyping ,
                               core:Toxicity ;
            core:itsComplianceIsSupportedWith indiv:AddNonToxicExamples ,
                                              indiv:AdversarialFDP ,
                                              indiv:AugmentedAntidoteData ,
                                              indiv:BlocklistDocumentRemoval ,
                                              indiv:CDA ,
                                              indiv:CalibratedReRanking ,
                                              indiv:ControlOffensiveTokens ,
                                              indiv:ListReAdjustment ,
                                              indiv:LogLikeDocumentRemoval ,
                                              indiv:PerceptronForUnawareness ,
                                              indiv:REALTOXICITYPROMPTS ,
                                              indiv:ReSamplingProtectedGroup ,
                                              indiv:RegularizationOnANOVA ,
                                              indiv:RegularizationOnValueFairness ,
                                              indiv:UserItemReRanking ;
            rdfs:comment "Requires providers of high-risk AI systems to establish, implement, document and maintain a risk management system to identify, analyse and mitigate risks to health, safety and fundamental rights, including discrimination. Notes: Art. 9 operationalises discrimination risk as a continuous iterative process across the entire lifecycle. Fairness notions/metrics are used as KRIs for risk identification/evaluation and drift monitoring; mitigation techniques are modelled as risk treatments with effectiveness evidenced through improvements in the corresponding metrics over time." .


